Cell["\<\
The algorithm recognizes the lattice metric and then reads a built-in path \
table covering 25 Brillouin-zone variations of the 14 three-dimensional \
Bravais lattice types.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ae2e9ec1-e163-4e1c-891d-5a48b360b204"],

Cell["\<\
This is not a space-group little-group or irreducible-representation \
calculation. Nonstandard primitive bases and centred-lattice conventions can \
prevent metric recognition; use an explicitly standardized basis or the \
matching BravaisType value.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"632dc392-667d-4fcb-8f62-1733dd5f1a9d"],

Cell["\<\
The returned path uses Bradley-Cracknell display labels where the \
correspondence is unambiguous, with Setyawan-Curtarolo labels retained as a \
fallback.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7119423d-0fa0-44c3-9b74-97e3d5aad48d"],

Cell["\<\
standardKPath returns $Failed and issues a message when no current model \
exists, the evaluated lattice is singular or nonnumeric, or the requested \
BravaisType conflicts with the recognized metric. It does not repair the \
input or switch to an approximate fallback.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4d7f41f1-a9cc-4544-bf6a-29de8d023d34"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "eb599e7a-7a7b-4fec-aa30-aea85dc81d0a"], "\"\<BravaisType\>\"", 
    "Automatic", Cell["\<\
Automatic metric recognition, or the matching recognized family/BZ string \
such as \"CubicPrimitive\" or \"CUB\".\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b800c767-625d-4a52-a397-01ca5d3ccef6"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "9e5ed9cc-78db-44c7-90f3-9509287e6557"], "\"\<Tolerance\>\"", 
    RowBox[{"10", "^", 
     RowBox[{"-", "6"}]}], Cell["\<\
Positive numerical tolerance used only in metric classification.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"111788f5-2b8d-4db5-9068-778d72745071"]}
  },
